## Computing Digit Sums

### Simple Digit Sum

```xiom
fn digit_sum(n: Int) -> Int {
  let mut sum = 0;
  let mut num = n;
  while num > 0 {
    sum += num % 10;
    num = num / 10;
  };
  sum
}
```

`num % 10` extracts the last digit. `num / 10` removes it. Repeat until nothing remains.

### Digital Root (Repeated Digit Sum)

```xiom
fn digital_root(n: Int) -> Int {
  let mut result = n;
  while result >= 10 {
    result = digit_sum(result);
  };
  result
}
```

### The Math Shortcut

The digital root of n equals `n % 9`, except when `n % 9 == 0`, then it's 9 (unless n=0).

```xiom
fn digital_root_math(n: Int) -> Int {
  if n == 0 { return 0; };
  if n % 9 == 0 { return 9; };
  n % 9
}
```

### Applications

- Check if a number is divisible by 3 (digit sum divisible by 3)
- Credit card validation (Luhn algorithm uses digit sums)
- Hash functions for uniform distribution

